--TEST--
The braced `namespace X { … }` form is refused — a namespace is a statement, and a file is one namespace
--FILE--
<?nvs
// ADR 0112 keys authority on the enclosing namespace and ADR 0104 keys an
// application on its entry file, so a file holding two namespaces has an
// authority that depends on the line number. The rewrite is one file each.
namespace App\Billing {
    class Invoice {
        public static function total(): int {
            return 1;
        }
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0243]: a `namespace` declaration is a statement, not a block
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
